  "description": "No two zebras have the same stripes, and their skin is dark under the fur. Camouflage and heat control were proposed, but the best-supported explanation is that stripes make it hard for horseflies to land; where flies are more common stripes tend to be bolder, and in an experiment horses wearing striped coats got far fewer landings. Unique patterns may also help with recognition. Original 3D animation; experiment bars are illustrative.",
